      "side": 1,
      "message": "Type safety: validators.email() raises on a non-string subject, turning a former 401 into an unhandled 500 (P2).\n\nPyJWT \u003e\u003d2.10 rejects a non-string sub at decode (InvalidSubjectError, caught by decode_auth_token -\u003e 401), but requirements.txt allows PyJWT\u003e\u003d2.6.0 and 2.6.0-2.9.x do not validate sub: a token signed with the (static, source-public) SECRET_KEY (config.py:5, no production override) and \"sub\": 123 decodes fine there, then email(123) raises AttributeError here - unhandled -\u003e 500. Pre-patch the same input hit find_user(email\u003d123), which returns an empty result and a clean 401. Minimal fix: `if not isinstance(resp, str) or not email(resp):` - this also captures the intent of the issue\u0027s isinstance suggestion while remaining type-safe.",
      "revId": "b6e6d76ac4f847cbc753a9f35ca3d41b1ebc8a7a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
